# MiniTorch does not read a .env file at runtime.
# This example exists so contributors do not invent a secrets layout.
#
# Copying this file to .env is optional and has no effect unless you
# add your own tooling.

# Helpful when running examples without `pip install -e .`
# PYTHONPATH=.

# NumPy / Python already honor these if you set them yourself:
# PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1

# Do not put API keys, tokens, or passwords here.
# MiniTorch artifacts must not store secrets.
